Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:01:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/33] Metal: fix w-layer inversion (transpose, kernel select,
 shifting phase)

Grid buffer was [v][u]-ordered but consumed as [u][v]: every image came
out transposed (peak exact, field scrambled). Fix all grid merge writes
and the degrid read to [u][v]; adjoint re-verified at 2.9e-07.

Cost-model port now matches ducc0's getNuNv exactly for w-gridding:
ndim=3 kernels, truncated plane count, rows*nchannels. A mismatched
kernel put the planes at the wrong spacing.

Apply ducc0's shifting phase exp(+2*pi*i*w*nshift) per visibility
before gridding (it is active whenever nshift != 0). Omitting it left
a w-proportional global phase per visibility: invisible at w = 0, a
~0.135 rad/lambda rotation elsewhere.

Host tile buckets now cover the full kernel window for odd support.
w-layer check: rel_rms ~1.3e-05 at w = 0,1,5,20,50,200 (was 2.6e-02
with peaks collapsed to 8%); 2-D path 1.4e-07.

